<Site title="Privacy Notice | Scornis Collaboration Inquiries" description="Learn how information submitted through the Scornis collaboration form is used to respond to inquiries, coordinate discussions, and manage profile review requests."><div class="wrap"><section class="page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Respect for your information</p><h1>Privacy notice.</h1><p>This notice describes the information collected through the Scornis inquiry form.</p></section><section class="section"><h2>Information you provide</h2><p>The form collects your name, professional email, optional organization, area of interest, project of interest, message, and consent. Please do not submit medical records, confidential research, passwords, or other sensitive information.</p><h2>How inquiries are handled</h2><p>Submissions are delivered to the site owner's account email and stored in the platform's inquiry dashboard. Scornis uses this information to respond to your inquiry, coordinate possible collaboration, and review profile or photograph requests.</p><h2>Your choices</h2><p>You can request correction or deletion of information, or withdraw consent to further correspondence, using the contact form. Include enough information to identify your inquiry without sharing unnecessary personal details.</p><h2>Photographs & professional profiles</h2><p>Team photographs and professional profile links are published only when supplied and approved. Profile changes can be requested through the contact form.</p><h2>External services</h2><p>The site uses hosted font resources and a platform-operated form service. Their handling of technical information is subject to their own service terms and privacy practices.</p><div class="buttons"><a class="button primary" href="/contact">Contact Scornis ↗</a></div></section></div></Site>